---
import { releaseScope as scope, sourceLink } from '../lib/coverage-data';
const bodyChecked = scope.body_counts.task_status.selected_body_copy_checked ?? 0;
---
<section aria-label="Selected verification scope" data-scope-table>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>{scope.proof_task_counts.selected}/{scope.body_counts.tasks}</strong> tasks have all current public entries in the selected proof build.</li>
    <li><strong>{bodyChecked}/{scope.body_counts.tasks}</strong> selected task bodies and <strong>{scope.examples.length}/{scope.body_counts.examples}</strong> worked examples have checked Python/Lean statement correspondence.</li>
    <li><strong>{scope.proof_task_counts.pending}</strong> task entry sets remain outside this release's proof gate.</li>
    <li><strong>{scope.pending_original_program_reviews}</strong> original-program acceptance reviews remain pending under the separate historical ledger.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The selected build contains {scope.root_count.toLocaleString()} root modules and {scope.source_dependency_count.toLocaleString()} local dependency files. Its CI builds those roots and audits every theorem's axiom dependencies, including private helpers. Read the linked contracts for input domains and the FP equivalence statements for numerical assumptions. This is not a native hardware or full-corpus acceptance certificate.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/VeriInfra-Lab/VeriTile/actions/workflows/verified-scope.yml">Check the selected proof run and its exact commit</a>. Website builds only check source fingerprints and inventory consistency.</p>
  <label>Find a task <input type="search" placeholder="e.g. softmax, layer_norm" data-scope-search /></label>
  <p data-scope-count role="status" aria-live="polite">{scope.tasks.length} tasks shown.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Task verification scope">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Selected proof build</th><th>Function body</th><th>Sources and public contracts</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {scope.tasks.map(row => <tr data-scope-row>
          <th scope="row">{row.task}</th>
          <td>{row.proof_scope === 'selected' ? 'Included' : 'Pending'}</td>
          <td>{row.body_status === 'selected_body_copy_checked' ? 'Statement correspondence checked' : 'Pending: uncovered JIT functions'}</td>
          <td><a href={sourceLink(row.python)}>Python</a>{' · '}<a href={sourceLink(row.kernel)}>Lean kernel</a>
            <ul>{row.entries.map(path => <li><a href={sourceLink(path)}>{path.split('/').at(-1)}</a></li>)}</ul>
          </td>
        </tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <details><summary>Worked examples and source provenance</summary>
    <ul>{scope.examples.map(row => <li><a href={sourceLink(row.lean)}>{row.name}</a>{' — '}{row.source_provenance.replaceAll('_', ' ')}{' · '}<a href={sourceLink(row.python)}>Python source</a></li>)}</ul>
    <p>Sources authored from independent mathematical specifications are identified separately from historical Python originals.</p>
  </details>
  <details><summary>Pending legacy checks</summary>
    <p>{scope.known_unselected_build_failures.length} old modules failed the broad integration build and are outside the selected release gate. Their sources and failed results remain available; they are not counted as verified by this release.</p>
    <ul>{Object.entries(scope.pending_python_tests).map(([name, reason]) => <li><code>{name}</code>: {reason}</li>)}</ul>
    <p><a href={sourceLink('bench/main-integration/README.md')}>Integration evidence and historical audit instructions</a></p>
  </details>
</section>
<script>
  function setup() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-scope-table]').forEach(root => {
      if (root.dataset.ready) return;
      root.dataset.ready = 'true';
      const search = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-scope-search]')!;
      const rows = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-scope-row]'));
      search.addEventListener('input', () => {
        const query = search.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase();
        let count = 0;
        for (const row of rows) {
          row.hidden = !row.textContent?.toLocaleLowerCase().includes(query);
          if (!row.hidden) count++;
        }
        root.querySelector('[data-scope-count]')!.textContent = `${count} of ${rows.length} tasks shown.`;
      });
    });
  }
  setup();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', setup);
</script>
<style>
  label { display: block; margin-block: 1.5rem .5rem; }
  input { display: block; padding: .6rem; width: min(100%, 26rem); font: inherit; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { display: table; width: 100%; min-width: 44rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  th, td { padding: .7rem; vertical-align: top; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  th[scope='row'] { font-family: inherit; text-transform: none; font-weight: 500; }
  td ul { padding-left: 1rem; margin-block: .5rem; }
  details { margin-block: 1.5rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; }
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }
</style>
